# 10. Dictionary Values Can Be Dictionaries

A dictionary can contain another dictionary.

This is called a **nested dictionary**.

Example:

```python
students = {
    "student1": {
        "name": "Niranjan",
        "age": 22
    },
    "student2": {
        "name": "Rahul",
        "age": 23
    }
}

print(students)
```

Accessing nested data:

```python
print(students["student1"]["name"])
```

Output:

```text
Niranjan
```

### Real-world use

Nested dictionaries are commonly useful for storing structured information such as:

```text
Company
 ├── Employee 1
 │    ├── Name
 │    ├── Age
 │    └── Salary
 │
 └── Employee 2
      ├── Name
      ├── Age
      └── Salary
```

